1. What is Docker?
Interview Answer (Simple)

Docker is an open-source platform that packages an application along with all its dependencies into a lightweight container. This ensures the application runs consistently across different environments, such as a developer's laptop, a test server, and production.

Real-World Example

Imagine you developed a Java application on your laptop.

It works perfectly.

You send it to the testing team.

They say:

"It doesn't work."

Why?

Because their server has:

Different Java version
Different libraries
Different operating system settings

Docker solves this by packaging everything the application needs into one container.

Wherever the container runs, it behaves the same way.

